  "notes_context": "These notes were distilled from earlier work in this repository that passed verification. Follow them unless the code or CHANGELOG.md shows they no longer hold.\n- [at-0001] Round money only with round_money: Always round monetary Decimal results with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0002] Use to_money and ZERO from ledgerly.money: Normalize line prices with ledgerly.money.to_money and seed sums with ledgerly.money.ZERO, as line_total and invoice_total in ledgerly/invoice.py do.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0003] Raise BillingError with machine-readable codes: Reject invalid billing input by raising BillingError(code, detail) from ledgerly.errors, using short snake_case codes like \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\" and \"negative_amount\"; never raise bare ValueError in ledgerly modules.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0004] Guard mutations with invoice.status draft check: Before mutating an invoice, check invoice.status != \"draft\" and raise BillingError(\"invalid_state\", f\"invoice {invoice.id} is {invoice.status}\"), matching issue_invoice in ledgerly/invoice.py.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)",
